# DataWeaver.AI mission
DataWeaver.AI is the persistent scientific context and memory layer of the Noricum platform: heterogeneous data integration, a canonical scientific domain model, first-class relationships, provenance/versioning, and a Scientific Context API consumed by Helix.AI.

> Helix owns reasoning and orchestration. DataWeaver owns persistent scientific context and memory. Helix never gets raw database access.

# Working plan
- Platform work follows `.cursor/plans/noricum-scientific-context-layer.md` (derived from the master plan in `Helix.AI/.cursor/plans/noricum-scientific-orchestration-platform.md`). Keep both in sync when either changes.
- Start substantial tasks in Plan Mode; save plans to `.cursor/plans/`.

# Primary objectives
- Safe, incremental, test-backed changes; root-cause fixes over patches.
- Strangler, not rewrite: new canonical tables beside legacy ones; compatibility adapters; no legacy migration or table retirement unless the plan says so.
- Preserve provenance, reproducibility and traceability (`trace_id` on every canonical record).

# Domain-model rules
- Shared domain objects arrive from Helix with their UUIDs; never mint IDs for them; duplicate id = integrity error.
- Context API writes are idempotent upserts (`PUT /api/context/<type>/{id}`); immutable types conflict with 409, versioned types create a new version.
- Every write creates its `ProvenanceEvent` and `relationships` edges in the same transaction.
- Persist structured rationale (`RationaleItem[]`), never free-text model reasoning.
- PostgreSQL + JSONB + a polymorphic `relationships` table; no graph database.

# Scope rules
- Do not silently broaden scope. Record related issues in `artifacts/worklog.md` and fix only if coupled to the current task.
- Existing `/api/bio/*`, `/api/workflows/*`, `/api/files/*` behaviour must not change unless the task says so.

# Safety rules
- Never use production secrets or production data; fixtures and `sample_data/` only.
- Never hardcode credentials, service keys or model keys; read from environment (`.env.example` documents names).
- Service auth (`X-Service-Key`) uses constant-time comparison.

# Testing and completion
- Run `cd backend && pytest tests/ -q` (SQLite) for every change; run the Postgres compose + `alembic upgrade head` before merging any migration.
- Regenerate `docs/openapi.yaml` when routers change; Helix consumes it as a fixture.
- A task is complete only when: tests pass, changed behaviour is covered by tests, results are written to `artifacts/test_results/`, and blockers are documented in `artifacts/worklog.md`.

# Canonical entry points
- `backend/main.py` (app, router mounting), `backend/app/database.py`, `backend/alembic/`
- Models: `backend/app/models/`, `backend/models/bio_entities.py` (legacy), `backend/app/models/knowledge/` (canonical, new)
- Services: `backend/app/services/` (analysis, matching, merging, QA), `backend/app/services/compat/` (legacy adapters, new)
- API: `backend/app/api/`, `backend/app/api/context/` (Scientific Context API, new)
